---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>Hi, I'm Suresh 👋</h1>
			<p>
				I'm a <strong>Sr. Site Reliability Engineer</strong> with a decade of experience owning and
				operating mission-critical Kubernetes platforms on AWS and GCP. I care deeply about
				observability, incident management, infrastructure automation, and zero-downtime operations.
			</p>
			<p>
				Lately I've been working on large-scale metrics systems (Cortex handling ~200M active
				series), Prometheus sharding, etcd-to-PostgreSQL migrations, and Terraform/Terragrunt
				automation for provisioning cloud infrastructure and edge locations.
			</p>
			<p>
				Right now I'm diving into <strong>AI and machine learning</strong>, and I'm documenting the
				journey here — learning in public. Expect notes on AI/ML fundamentals, LLMs, and how these
				tools intersect with infrastructure and reliability, alongside the SRE topics I know well:
				scaling observability stacks, running Kubernetes at the edge, and Go tooling.
			</p>
			<p>
				Have a look at the <a href="/blog">blog</a>, or read more <a href="/about">about me</a>.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
